'''Abysses''' are interactable objects in instances which spawns cracks and pits that spawn monsters. They can spawn from [[Act 6]] onwards. This encounter is considered [[Extra Content]] and has a baseline greater than 8% chance to appear in any [[map]] area.

Abyss monsters can also be found in Abyssal Depths biomes in [[Delve]].

==Overview==
Abysses spawn from [[Act 6]] onwards and in [[map]]s. Abysses are marked on the minimap with a green icon {{mico|size=small|id=Abyss}}.

Abyss encounters spawn as multiple abyssal pits with multiple fissures branching from each. The abyss cracks absorb the lifeforce of native monsters in the area, indicated by a green glow. Killing monsters close to these fissures will send their souls to the abyss and close up the cracks. Once the fissures have closed all the way to the pit, the pit will activate and spawn a large number of Abyssal monsters, with rarities and modifiers based on the rarities and modifiers of the slain weakened monsters. Each Abyss encounter will spawn Abyss monsters aligned with one of the Abyssal Liches: Amanamu, Ulaman, or Kurgal.

Once most of the emerging Abyssal monsters have been killed, the pit will close up. The pit will often spawn a [[chest]] that contains items. The primary loot from these chests depend on its type:
* Abyssal Armoury: Armour
* Abyssal Arsenal: Weapons
* Abyssal Cache
* Abyssal Chest: Assorted items
* Abyssal Coffer: Currency 
* Abyssal Jewellery: Jewellery
* Abyssal Treasures
* Abyssal Trove: Abyss jewels
Some chests will appear as a Greater version that drop more items. Abyss encounters will always spawn at least one Greater chest.

Item drops from Abyssal chests are biased towards certain types depending on the Abyssal Lich the spawned monsters were aligned with:
* Amanamu: Armour, {{il|Ghastly Eye Jewel}}
* Ulaman: Jewellery, {{il|Murderous Eye Jewel}}, {{il|Searching Eye Jewel}}
* Kurgal: Weapons, {{il|Hypnotic Eye Jewel}}

In zone levels 78 and up, a pit may instead open an entrance to the [[Abyssal Depths]], containing an encounter with one of two [[Abyssal Depths#Abyssal Liches|Abyssal Liches]].

If an area already has an Abyss, modifiers that cause areas to contain additional Abysses will instead add two additional pits.

==Related items==
===Abyss Jewels===
{{main|Abyss jewel}}
[[Abyss jewel]]s are a type of [[jewel]]. They roll different modifiers than ones found in regular jewels that have tiers that are [[item level]] dependent. They can be socketed into jewel sockets on the passive tree, as well as items that have an [[abyssal socket]].

===Stygian Vise===
{{il|Stygian Vise}} is a [[belt]] with an abyssal socket as its implicit, allowing it to be socketed with an abyss jewel. Stygian Vises drop from the [[Abyssal Depths#Abyssal Liches|Abyssal Lich]] boss in [[Abyssal Depths]].

