==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.29.2|
* Increased the Quantity of Items dropped and Experience granted by slain elite Abyss monsters.
* Abysses no longer spawn inside Breach Hive encounters.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.29.1|
* Enabled the [[Abyssal Bloodline]] class.
* Abyssal Depths Lich bosses no longer have immunity phases where you have to defeat Stygian Spires in three side rooms.
* Abyssal Depths Lich boss life has been increased by 25% to partially account for the overall shortening of the fight.
* Abyssal Depths Lich boss fights have an additional arena mechanic where crystal spires will periodically fire beams towards each other.
* After killing a boss in an Abyssal Depths there are now 3 chests granting a variety of valuable rewards.
* Reduced the variance in number of drops and increased the quality/quantity of rewards from Abyss chests, particularly those that drop Currency and Scarabs.
* There is now a larger difference in the rarity and quantity of items dropped from Greater Abyssal Chests compared to their corresponding non-Greater versions.
* Passive skill tree nodes that have been affected by an Abyss Jewel now have unique border visuals.
* Added keywords for the Ulaman, Kurgal and Amanamu factions on the Atlas passive tree.
* Updated the Abyss encounter minimap icons to match those in Path of Exile 2.
* {{Ruthless}} Fixed a bug which allowed non-Ruthless varieties of Abyssal Coffers to spawn in Ruthless.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.29.0|
* Abyss has received function changes to the mechanic to improve the gameplay significantly.
* Abyssal Pits, and the cracks leading up to them, are now already opened before you approach, subjugating the souls of the enemies unlucky enough to be within its influence.
* Slaying these enemies sends their souls into the pit, drawing the attention and ire of the minions of Kulemak dwelling beneath. Upon slaying enough of them, the Abyssal legion will spill forth from their domain.
* Gone are the days of chasing a meandering Abyssal crack around a Map, often backwards.
* Abyss is now the exclusive source of [[Abyssal Jewel|Abyssal Jewels]] and {{il|Stygian Vise|Stygian Vises}}, though Abyssal Jewels can still be obtained rarely within Abyss Biomes in Delve.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.21.0|
* Abyssal Depths now always contain a Lich. Because the rate of encountering Abyssal Liches is unchanged, Abyssal Depths are rarer than before.
* It is now possible for a Stygian Spire to spawn in the place of an Abyssal Trove at the end of an Abyss, which will drop all of the jewels and other items you would normally receive as well as a Stygian Vise.
* Abyssal Depths can now only appear in level 78 or above areas (previously 70 or above).
* Abyssal Depths now always spawn at the fourth hole, if they were going to spawn at all, instead of immediately after a single hole.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.20.0|
* We want to improve on the concept that the Atlas Tree allows players to invest into leagues that they enjoy, and have added new clusters to the passive tree for league content that can be blocked through Atlas Passive Skills. We've also increased the chances for such league content to appear.
* Reworked the Abyss Clusters on the Atlas Passive Tree in lieu of the combat changes made to Abysses.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.14.0|
* Reduced the chance for Map Areas to contain [[Abyss]], [[Strongbox|Ambush]], [[Blight (game mechanic)|Blight]], [[Breach (original)|Breach]], [[Shrine|Domination]], [[Essence]], [[Smuggler's Cache|Heist]], [[Legion]], [[Metamorph]] and [[Tormented spirit|Torment]] encounters by 20%. The chance to encounter a Zana mission containing any of these mechanics has also been lowered by the same amount.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.12.1|
* Fixed a bug where Abysses sometimes did not spawn their chests.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.11.0|
* The area transition to an [[Abyssal Depths]] area now becomes interactable more quickly after appearing.
* [[Monsters]], crystals and other [[boss]] encounter elements are now destroyed when {{c|unique|'''[[Amanamu]]'''}} is defeated.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.2.0|
* Abyss has been rolled into the core game! You can now encounter Abysses in the world from [[Part II]] onwards. Each area has approximately a 10% chance to spawn an Abyss.
* [[Abyssal Depths]] can no longer appear in areas below level 70.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.1.0|
* With 3.1.0, there are Standard and Hardcore variations of the Abyss challenge league available, as well as solo self-found variants of both. They have the same core mechanics and items. In the Abyss League, players will encounter '''cracks in the ground'''. Get too close, and these cracks widen and spread, allowing the terrible monsters to climb from their inky depths. Pursue these cracks, and you may discover a massive chasm from which dangerous packs of monsters emerge. Once you defeat these monsters, the '''Abyss''' continues to propagate, creating more chasms. Take too long, and the Abyss will seal shut, but if you're quick and deadly enough, a chest filled with valuable rewards will emerge from below.
* As players progress through the Abyss League, some pits may offer access to the Abyssal Depths below. These Abyssal Depths are packed with monstrous creatures and valuable rewards, and culminate in an exciting boss encounter.
* Monsters and chests from the '''Abyss''' can drop Abyss Jewels. Like other Jewels, these can be placed in sockets in your passive tree to grant powerful bonuses. Unlike other Jewels, they have a set of exclusive new properties and can also be placed in Abyssal Sockets on your items! These sockets can be found on the new Abyss Uniques and a new base type of Abyss-socketed belt: the Stygian Vise.
}}
